IMPLEMENTATION RECEIPT 2026-08-29 — LIVE MAPPLUTO V3 SOURCE-PLANE BRIDGE

Upstream capability changed materially. Fresh cmdrvl-data MCP/Snowflake reads verified EDGAR_DB.SOURCE.NYC_DCP_MAPPLUTO_GEOM_V3_EXT plus its geometry-evidence and transform-receipt siblings. Counts are 856,614 rows for 26v1 and 856,687 for 26v2 on both source and derived geometry planes, with no null source/derived geometry hashes in the geometry plane and no null source/derived WKB in the evidence plane. A bounded 500-row locator join agreed on BBL and both hashes. This is live v3 proof, not the old HOT/v2 fixture claim.

Canon now ships canon geo materialize-warehouse-geometry --rows. It:
- reads an offline release-pinned warehouse-row artifact and never reaches the network;
- recomputes each canonical base64 ISO-WKB SHA-256 before decoding;
- supports 2D ISO Point, Polygon, and MultiPolygon and refuses malformed/unsupported WKB;
- refuses mixed release/date/archive/geometry-contract/CRS/SRID/transform execution sets;
- exactly quantizes IEEE-754 source coordinates to a declared fixed-decimal lattice with ties-to-even and an exact per-row loss fraction;
- maps EPSG:2263 source units to local millimetres with the exact US-survey-foot ratio 1,200,000 / 3,937;
- requires an explicit stable versioned source origin, so accreting later rows cannot shift prior canonical coordinates or the frame digest;
- delegates to the existing canonical topology, normalization, bbox, vertex, and tile-byte budget kernel;
- keeps WKB-to-decimal admission loss separate from local-mm snap loss and preserves WGS84 transform ids only as sibling-plane provenance.

Fresh live 26v2 row: source record 26v2/mn/000000/1, BBL 1000010100.0, declared/recomputed WKB SHA-256 5ed87d37d872789086452c35f658f5628ba870ca36072c495bb88519592403ed. Results: 20 decoded vertices -> 19 canonical vertices; max WKB-to-9-decimal error 945/2048 fixed nanofeet, conservatively 1 micrometre; max local-mm snap 491 micrometres; exact source affine 3 / 9,842,500 mm per fixed unit; local affine projection error 0. Two fresh processes emitted identical bytes, SHA-256 b090c157aa37cd72c67d726f2f5bf9f829e9ff9e00b297769368626bb444ec59.

Negative coverage includes digest drift, noncanonical base64, unsupported WKB, mixed transform execution, malformed oversized container counts refusing before allocation, topology defects, and the accretion invariant that adding a second row under the same explicit origin leaves the first feature and frame unchanged.

Local gate: cargo fmt --check; cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings; full cargo test all green. Targeted contract/schema/safety suites also green.

Honest boundary: exactness is relative to verified WKB -> declared 9-decimal source lattice -> local integer millimetres. This does not prove source survey accuracy, world truth, all-row validity, candidate reach, H3 parity, or area-majority clipping. Remote Linux/macOS CI for this pushed change remains to be observed before final closure.
